{"id": 35, "ts": 1779925315.5622792, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I agree with the panel\u2019s current leaning toward **Candidate\u202fA**. The recent confirmations that we also lack explicit crew\u2011cooperation observations for Candidate\u202fD (and still for B and C) mean that A is not uniquely missing this data; the only concrete crew\u2011cooperation concerns we have are the \u201cuncooperative\u201d label for B and the egocentric, communication\u2011difficulty notes for C, plus the arrogance and weak leadership noted for D. Likewise, while we still have no direct evidence of A\u2019s stress resilience, B\u2019s stress handling is the only positive signal we possess, but it is offset by his uncooperative demeanor. Given A\u2019s strong technical profile\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision, and very good leadership\u2014combined with the absence of any concrete crew\u2011cooperation or stress\u2011resilience red flags (unlike the explicit concerns for the other candidates), I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fA**. We should continue to seek the missing observations, but the balance of evidence still favors A."}
